desc:Volca Drum Panel
// VOLCA DRUM PANEL 1.5 by NH4X - editor + display for the Korg volca drum, as one JSFX.
// Music: https://nh4x.bandcamp.com/
//
// SETUP
//  1. Install via ReaPack, or put this file into REAPER's Effects folder (Options > Show REAPER resource path > Effects),
//     then add "JS: Volca Drum Panel" to a track.
//  2. Track: MIDI hardware output = the port your volca drum is connected to.
//  3. Volca: split channel mode (part 1-6 = MIDI channel 1-6, see the Korg manual). Waveguide CCs go out on channel 1.
//  4. FILT and CLIP (purple row names) need the custom firmware "vdcf" by hj-oja (CC 54/55);
//     on the stock Korg firmware they do nothing. Everything else works on stock firmware.
//
// USE
//  - Drag or mouse wheel = change, double-click = default, hover + type 0-127 + Enter = exact value.
//    Rest the mouse 1 s on a button = what it does (in the display).
//  - SELECT is shown as three rows: SRC (source), MOD.T (modulation type), EG.T (envelope type).
//    Each row changes only its own part (click a segment, drag or wheel). Still one Select CC underneath.
//  - The volca has no MIDI out: the panel only knows what it sent. SEND ALL pushes the whole kit
//    (nothing is sent when a project loads).
//  - Kits = REAPER presets of this plugin (preset menu at the top of the FX window). Loading one sends the changes.
//  - Click a part title = select that part. LINK = changes on one layer go to the other layer too.
//    Play button = one test hit on that part. Q = pitch quantize (QPI, CC 53) for that part.
//  - SOUND (or right-click a part title): copy a part, paste it into another part (also across kits).
//  - RANDOM: target (part / layer / kit), amount, ROLL, UNDO (also undoes a paste; press again = redo).
//    Locks (amber) are skipped by every roll: right-click (or Shift+click) a bar = one cell,
//    click a row name = that row in this part, right-click a row name = that row in all parts,
//    Shift+click a part title = whole part. Locks are saved with the project, not in presets.
//  - MORPH: SET A, SET B (snapshots of the whole kit, saved with the project), then move the bar.
//    Select and WG Model switch at 50 %. Locked cells don't move. Tip: set A and B from two saved kits.
//  - LOOK (small square, top left) = Classic / Sleeve. COLOR (swatch next to it) = 14 color themes (click or wheel).
//    Sleeve uses the free font "Big Shoulders Display" if installed (Google Fonts), otherwise Bahnschrift Condensed.
//  - Note routing: notes 65/67/69/71/72/74 on any channel go out on channel 1-6 (= part 1-6),
//    so one piano roll on one channel plays all parts. Notes on channel 11-16 go to part 1-6 unchanged
//    (play a part melodically, best with Q on). All other MIDI passes through.
//  - All parameters are plugin parameters: automation and MIDI controllers (e.g. ReaLearn) work.
//    Sliders 146 Roll / 147 Undo act as buttons (1 = fire), 148 = Morph.
//
// COMING WITH THE VOLCA DRUM SEQUENCER RELEASE (same ReaPack repository):
//  sound files (SAVE / LOAD / RENAME / DELETE a part in the SOUND menu), kit scripts (save / next / previous kit,
//  kit names in the display and in MORPH), kit per sequencer pattern, p-locks from the sequencer, Q following the
//  sequencer's pitch lanes. Until then these parts of the panel simply stay quiet.
//
// CC numbers: Korg "volca drum MIDI Implementation Chart (Split channel)" 2019.2.20 + vdcf README (54 FLT, 55 CLP),
// QPI CC 53 from the Synthmata volca drum editor. Fonts: Bahnschrift + Consolas (Windows).

options:no_meter gmem=NH4XVolca
in_pin:none
out_pin:none

